          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#LocAndTopology Localizations and Grothendieck topology
          %p
            We reproduce the proof that the two characterization in def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoryOfSheaves"}
            above are indeed equivalent.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-site"} (∞,1)-site
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} sub-(∞,1)-category
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+objects"} local objects
              with respect to the covering monomorphisms in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)
              is indeed a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+localization"} topological localization
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
              is indeed an exact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} reflective sub-(∞,1)-category
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)
              and hence an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
          %p
            This is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, Prop. 6.2.2.7
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              We must prove that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheafification"} (∞,1)-sheafification
              functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \colon PSh(C)\to Sh(C)
              preserves
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limits"} finite (∞,1)-limits
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\in PSh(C)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^+
              by the formula
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mi U
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo ←
                      %mrow
                        %mi u
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi U
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^+(c)={\lim_{\rightarrow}}_U {\lim_{\leftarrow}}_{u\in U} F(u)
            %p
              where the colimit is taken over all covering sieves
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              of
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plus+construction"} plus construction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)\to PSh(C)
              and there is an obvious morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\to F^+
              natural in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %p
              It is clear that the construction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\mapsto F^+
              preserves
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limits"} finite (∞,1)-limits
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimits"} filtered (∞,1)-colimits
              do, and it is easy to see that the map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\to F^+
              becomes an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} equivalence
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinal"} ordinal
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^{(\alpha)}
              be the
              = succeed "-iteration" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plus+construction"} plus construction
              applied to the presheaf
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\mapsto F^{(\alpha)}
              preserves finite limits and the canonical map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\to F^{(\alpha)}
              becomes an equivalence in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^{(\alpha)}
              is a sheaf, then
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi F
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi α
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^{(\alpha)}\simeq L(F)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              such that, for every
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\in PSh(C)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^{(\alpha)}
              is a sheaf.
            %p
              Fix
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c\in C
              and a covering sieve
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G\in PSh(C/c)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Match
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Match(U,G)\in PSh(C/c)
              by the formula
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Match
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi d
                    %mo →
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo ←
                      %mrow
                        %mi u
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                        %mi U
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Match(U,G)(f: d\to c)={\lim_{\leftarrow}}_{u\in f^\ast U}G(u).
            %p
              Restriction maps induce a morphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi θ
                        %mi G
                      %mo :
                      %mi G
                      %mo →
                      %mi Match
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo ,
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_G: G\to Match(U,G)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ∼
                    %mi Match
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G(u)\stackrel{\sim}{\to} Match(U,G)(u)
              for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi u
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u\in U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Match
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Match(U,-)
              is
              %em idempotent
              in the sense that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Match
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Match(U,\theta_G)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mrow
                        %mi Match
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo ,
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_{Match(U,G)}
              are (equivalent) equivalences.
            %p
              By definition,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\in PSh(C)
              is a sheaf if and only if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ∼
                    %mi Match
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi F
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(c)\stackrel{\sim}{\to} Match(U,F|_{C/c})(c)
              for every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c\in C
              and every covering sieve
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              (depending only on the (∞,1)-site
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\in PSh(C)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Match
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^{(\alpha)}(c) \to \Match(U,F^{(\alpha)}|_{C/c})(c)
            %p is an equivalence.
            %p
              The morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi G
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G\to G^+
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C/c)
              factors as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mi Match
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi G
                      %mo +
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G\to Match(U,G)\to G^+.
            %p
              Applying
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Match
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Match(U,-)
              to this factorization, we get a commutative diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi G
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Match
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo ,
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi G
                              %mo +
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi θ
                                    %mi G
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi θ
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi Match
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                      %mi U
                                      %mo ,
                                      %mi G
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi θ
                                    %mrow
                                      %msup
                                        %mi G
                                        %mo +
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Match
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo ,
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Match
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Match
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo ,
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Match
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo ,
                            %msup
                              %mi G
                              %mo +
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    G &amp;\to&amp; Match(U,G) &amp;\to&amp; G^+
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\theta_G}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\theta_{Match(U,G)}}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\theta_{G^+}}}
                    \\\
                    Match(U,G) &amp;\to&amp; Match(U,Match(U,G)) &amp;\to&amp; Match(U,G^+)
                    }
            %p
              in which the map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mrow
                        %mi Match
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo ,
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_{Match(U,G)}
              is an equivalence since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Match
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Match(U,-)
              is idempotent. By cofinality, the colimit of the maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi G
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_{G^{(n)}}
              as
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\to\infty
              is an equivalence. Applying this to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo =
                      %mi F
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G=F|_{C/c}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ω
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ∼
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo →
                        %mn ∞
                    %mi Match
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^{(\omega)}(c)\stackrel{\sim}{\to} {\lim_{\rightarrow}}_{n\to\infty} Match(U,F^{(n)}|_{C/c})(c).
            %p
              This
              %em almost
              means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ω
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^{(\omega)}
              is a sheaf. The problem is that the filtered colimit on the right-hand side need not commute with the limit appearing in the definition of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Match
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Match(U,-)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi ω
                    %mi Match
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Match
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ω
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\lim_{\rightarrow}}_{\alpha \lt \omega} Match(U,F^{(\alpha)}|_{C/c})(c) \to \Match(U,F^{(\omega)}|_{C/c})(c)
            %p
              need not be an equivalence. To solve this problem, we choose a cardinal
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              such that for every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c\in C
              and every covering sieve
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Match
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi Psh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Match(U,(-)|_{C/c})(c):Psh(C)\to \infty Grpd
              preserves
              = succeed "-filtered" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is small and each of these functors, being the composition of the restriction functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)\to PSh(U)
              and the limit functor
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi Grpd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(U)\to\infty Grpd
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} adjoint (∞,1)-functor
              and is therefore accessible (see
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HTT"} HTT Prop. 5.4.7.7
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
              replaced by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              is an equivalence. For every ordinal
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha\lt\kappa
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^{(\alpha)}
              shows that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi α
                        %mo +
                        %mi ω
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ∼
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo →
                        %mn ∞
                    %mi Match
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi α
                        %mo +
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^{(\alpha+\omega)}(c)\stackrel{\sim}{\to} {\lim_{\rightarrow}}_{n\to\infty} Match(U,F^{(\alpha+n)}|_{C/c})(c),
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              is a limit ordinal, we deduce that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi κ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^{(\kappa)}
              is a sheaf by cofinality.
          %p And conversely:
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (equivalence of site structures and categories of sheaves)
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} small (∞,1)-category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-site"} (∞,1)-site
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and equivalence classes of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+localization"} topological localization
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop. 6.2.2.9
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              a small
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-site"} (∞,1)-site
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi L
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C) \stackrel{\overset{L}{\leftarrow}}{\hookrightarrow} PSh(C)
              the corressponding reflective inclusion of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-sheaves
              into
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-presheaves
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              we have that the image under
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              of a sub-
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              \-functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : U \to j(c)
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j(c)
              is covering precisely if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(p)
              is an equivalence.
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, lemma 6.2.2.8
          .proof
            %h6#proof_of_the_lemma Proof of the Lemma
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
              is the reflectuive localization of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)
              at covering monomorphisms, it is clear that if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : U \to j(c)
              is covering, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(p)
              is an equivalence.
            %p
              To see the converse, form the 0-truncation of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L i
              and conclude as for ordinary sheaves on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} homotopy catgegory
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %p …
          .proof
            %h6#proof_of_the_proposition Proof of the Proposition
            %p
              We have seen in (…) that for every structure of an
              = succeed "-site" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              we obtain a topological localization of the presheaf category, and that this is an injective map from site structures to equivalence classes of sheaf categories. It remains to show that it is also a surjective map, i.e. that every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+localization"} topological localization
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)
              comes from the structure of an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-site"} (∞,1)-site
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %p
              So consider
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subset Mor(PSh(C))
              a strongly saturated class of morphisms which s topological (closed under pullbacks). Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_0 \subset S
              for the subcalss of those that are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} monomorphisms
              of the form
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo →
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \to j(c)
            %p
              Observe that then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is indeed generated by (is the smallest strongly saturated class containing)
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_0
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-Yoneda+lemma"} co-Yoneda lemma
              every object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in PSh(C)
              is a colimit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mi k
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Ξ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \simeq {\lim_\to}_k j(\Xi_k)
              over representables. It follows that every monomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : Y \to X
              is a colimit (in
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Func
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ,
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Func(\Delta[1],PSh(C))
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo →
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \to j(c)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi f
                              %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                                %munder
                                  %mi lim
                                  %mo →
                              %mi k
                            %msub
                              %mi Ξ
                              %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ≃
                                  %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                                %munder
                                  %mi lim
                                  %mo →
                              %mi k
                            %msub
                              %mi Ξ
                              %mi k
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                                %munder
                                  %mi lim
                                  %mo →
                              %mi k
                            %msup
                              %mi f
                              %mo *
                            %msub
                              %mi Ξ
                              %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ≃
                                  %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                                %munder
                                  %mi lim
                                  %mo →
                              %mi k
                            %msub
                              %mi Ξ
                              %mi k
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    f^* ({\lim_\to}_k \Xi_k) &amp;\to&amp; Y
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\simeq f}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                    \\\
                    {\lim_\to}_k \Xi_k &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}&amp; X
                    }
                    \\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\simeq
                    \\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\array{
                    ({\lim_\to}_k f^* \Xi_k) &amp;\to&amp; Y
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\simeq f}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                    \\\
                    {\lim_\to}_k \Xi_k &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}&amp; X
                    }
            %p
              where the equivalence is due to the fact that we have
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+colimits"} universal colimits
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              as a colimit over morphisms of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Ξ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Ξ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^* j(\Xi_k) \to j(\Xi_k)
              that are each a pullback of a monomorphism. Since monomorphisms are stable under pullback (see
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} monomorphism in an (∞,1)-category
              for details), all these component morphisms are themselves monomorphisms.
            %p
              So every monomorphism in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is generated from
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is topological, it is itself entirely generated from monomorphisms, hence is generated from
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_0
            %p
              So far this establishes that evry topological localization of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)
              is a localization at a collection of sieves/ subfunctors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \to j(c)
              of representables. It remains to show that this collection of subfunctors is indeed an Grothendieck topology and hence exhibits on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              the structure of an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-site"} (∞,1)-site
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %em equivalences cover
                  – The equivalences
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mo ≃
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j(c) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} j(c)
                  belong to
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  and are monomorphisms, hence belong to
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi S
                            %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_0
              %li
                %p
                  %em pullback of a cover is covering
                  \- Since monomorphisms are stable under pullback, we haave for every
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo :
                        %mi U
                        %mo →
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : U \to j(c)
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  and every
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j(f) : j(d) \to j(c)
                  that also the pullback
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^* p
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo *
                                %mi U
                              %mtd
                                %mo →
                              %mtd
                                %mi U
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %msup
                                        %mi f
                                        %mo *
                                      %mi p
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mi p
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi j
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi d
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo →
                                  %mi f
                              %mtd
                                %mi j
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi c
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        f^* U &amp;\to&amp; U
                        \\\
                        \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{f^* p}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                        \\\
                        j(d) &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; j(c)
                        }
                %p
                  is a monomorphism and in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi S
                            %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_0
              %li
                %p
                  %em if restriction of a sieve to a cover is covering, then the sieve is covering
                  – Let
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo :
                        %mi U
                        %mo →
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : U \to j(c)
                  be an arbitrary monomorphism and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
